Subject: [PATCH 1/6] docs(cdd/review): add honest-claim verification rule
 (3.13)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a new verdict rule to cdd/review/SKILL.md for verifying that
documents claim only what code/data/canonical-source backs:

  3.13(a) Reproducibility — every quoted measurement is reproducible
          from artifacts in this commit
  3.13(b) Source-of-truth alignment — every term in a non-spec doc
          traces to canonical definition
  3.13(c) Wiring claims — grep-verify that 'X is wired into Y' claims
          actually appear in Y's call graph

Adds 'honest-claim' to the finding taxonomy and the pre-publish
checklist.

Motivation: the cnos-tsc supercycle (master usurobor/tsc#23) surfaced
this pattern across multiple cycles. Three of four findings on the
v3.2.0 self-coherence report cycle were honest-claim violations
(undeclared artifact, score discrepancy, missing provenance). Making
the implicit rule explicit gives beta a checkable sub-procedure and
gives alpha a target to write toward.

Severity: each sub-check is binding (D-level) when violated.
